---
import PageLayout from '../../layouts/PageLayout.astro';
---

<PageLayout
  title="Volunteer With Us | Silver Lining of Hope"
  description="Volunteer with Silver Lining of Hope: case research, data work on The Missing Link, events, writing, and trained family outreach roles in Indiana."
  heading="Volunteer"
  intro="You don't need a badge or a degree. You need care, discipline, and a few hours."
  crumbs={[
    { label: 'Get involved', href: '/get-involved' },
    { label: 'Volunteer', href: '/get-involved/volunteer' },
  ]}
>
  <div class="container--narrow section prose">
    <h2>Volunteer roles</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Research volunteers</strong> — public records requests, database cross-referencing, and timeline work under our methodology. Detail-oriented people thrive here.</li>
      <li><strong>The Missing Link data team</strong> — compiling and cleaning Indiana missing person records for <a href="/programs/the-missing-link">the directory</a>. Remote-friendly.</li>
      <li><strong>Event support</strong> — setup, logistics, and hospitality at vigils, walks, and fundraisers.</li>
      <li><strong>Writers &amp; communicators</strong> — plain-language guides, blog posts, and social content that informs without sensationalizing.</li>
      <li><strong>Family outreach (trained)</strong> — after training, supporting families as a steady, trauma-informed presence alongside our advocates.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>What we ask of every volunteer</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Confidentiality — you'll sign an agreement, and we mean it. Families trust us with the worst thing that ever happened to them.</li>
      <li>Respect — no true-crime tourism, no speculation about open cases, on or off the clock.</li>
      <li>Reliability — a few consistent hours beat many promised ones.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>How to join</h2>
    <p>
      <a href="/about/contact">Contact us</a> with the role you're interested
      in and a sentence or two about yourself. We'll set up a conversation,
      and for case-adjacent roles, a background check and training. Most
      volunteers start on The Missing Link data team — it's meaningful,
      structured, and the fastest way to learn how this work is done well.
    </p>
  </div>
</PageLayout>
